You know, I've started abandoning my pets at first opportunity.  Either
they've gotten wimpier since the days of hack, or the monsters have gotten
tougher, because they tend to die very easily if you don't consciously build
them up.  I remember when I used to walk onto a new level in terror that I'd
get killed by a dog from a bones file if I didn't have a tripe ration.  Now,
little dogs aren't much harder to kill than rats.

The upshot of this is that they don't serve much purpose as an aid to defense.
The exception is, of course, if your pet gets polymorphed into something nasty,
which creates its own problem.  I had a dog turn into a Marilith which proceed-
ed to toast every shopkeeper in the game and the only priest I could find with
the same alignment as mine.

Minor spoilers re: pets and altars follow:


The next use for a pet is to tell if something's cursed.  It's not 100%
reliable, takes a long time, and won't tell you if something's cursed.  Once
I discovered that dropping things on altars tells you their blessed/cursed
status, there went that reason.  I can always find at least one altar.

The only other reason for pets is to steal stuff from shops without being
punished...  I've found that it takes so long to get anything of use in most
cases that I end up either starving to death or giving up...

Is there some other use for pets?

